SESSION 1 — Resource Group, VNet, Subnet, NSG
============================================================

Created Resource Group:

Command:
az group create --name az-net-lab-rg --location centralindia --tags owner=tarun

Result:
    provisioningState: Succeeded
    name: az-net-lab-rg
    location: centralindia

Observed tags:
    AutoDelete: Yes
    owner: tarun
    CreatedOn: <Azure-generated timestamp>


------------------------------------------------------------
Resource Group inspection
------------------------------------------------------------

Command:
az group show -n az-net-lab-rg -o table

Result:
    Location       Name
    centralindia   az-net-lab-rg

Note:
    Default table output does not display tags.

Attempted JMESPath query:

az group show -n az-net-lab-rg \
    --query "{Name:name, Location:location, Tags;tags}" \
    -o table

Result:
    Invalid JMESPath expression.

Cause:
    Used ';' instead of ':' in the object projection.

Correct query:

az group show -n az-net-lab-rg \
    --query "{Name:name, Location:location, Tags:tags}" \
    -o json

Result:
    Tags were displayed correctly.

More focused query:

az group show -n az-net-lab-rg \
    --query "{Name:name, Location:location, Owner:tags.owner, Autodelete:tags.AutoDelete}" \
    -o table

Result:
    Name           Location       Owner    Autodelete
    az-net-lab-rg  centralindia   tarun    Yes

Learning:
    JMESPath object keys on the left side are user-defined aliases.
    The value on the right side references the Azure JSON property.


